Subject: [PATCH 5.15.y 0/9] can: bcm: backport of 9 patches that failed to
 apply to 5.15-stable

This resubmits "can: bcm: add locking when updating filter and timer
values" (commit 749179c2e25b95d22499ed29096b3e02d6dfd2b4 upstream),
which failed to apply to the 5.15-stable tree, together with 8
further bcm.c patches from the same upstream series that build on it
and would otherwise fail for the same reason. This is the full set
of 11 upstream bcm.c patches from 7.2-rc3 minus the 2 already queued
by the normal stable process for 5.15 ("can: bcm: fix lockless
bound/ifindex race and silent RX_SETUP failure", "can: bcm: add
missing rcu list annotations and operations").

As on 5.10.y, patch 1/9 ("defer rx_op deallocation to workqueue") is
also adapted here, unlike on newer branches (6.1.y and later) where
it applies unmodified: 5.15-stable never received the unrelated
commit edd1a7e42f1d2 ("can: bcm: registration process optimization
in bcm_module_init()", no Cc: stable), which reworked
bcm_module_init()/bcm_module_exit() into a goto-based, error-checked
unwind chain. This patch's workqueue-cleanup addition is applied
directly to the older, unrefactored module_init/module_exit
structure instead; see the patch changelog for details.

Patches 2, 3, 8 and 9 differ from their upstream commits the same
way as on 6.6.y/5.10.y: upstream additionally threads a
traffic_flags/RX_LOCAL/RX_OWN computation through bcm_rx_handler(),
introduced by commit fec846fa7eddf7bb651bf88bd78c7db1410ae3b1 ("can:
bcm: add recvmsg flags for own, local and remote traffic"), which is
not present on 5.15-stable and not itself a stable candidate (pure
feature addition, no Cc: stable). The traffic_flags-related hunks
are omitted in each of these four patches; the actual fixes they
contain are unaffected and fully applied. Patch 2/9 also required
the same manual re-anchor in bcm_rx_thr_handler() as on 5.10.y.

Patch 6/9 ("add missing device refcount for CAN filter removal") is
additionally adapted: upstream uses the netdevice_tracker/
netdev_hold()/netdev_put() debug-tracking infra, which is not
available on 5.15-stable. Replaced with the plain, always-available
dev_hold()/dev_put(), which is functionally identical for the actual
fix (holding a reference across a concurrent NETDEV_UNREGISTER) -
just without the extra leak-tracking instrumentation. This mirrors
the same adaptation on 5.10.y, made after an actual build failure was
reported there ("error: unknown type name 'netdevice_tracker'"); this
revision has been verified with a clean git am against a seeded
net/can/bcm.c and no longer references that type anywhere in the
result.

Patches 4-7 are unmodified backports that apply cleanly once 2/9 is
in place; they were previously reported as FAILED for the same
underlying reason (missing bcm_rx_update_lock prerequisite), not for
independent conflicts.

This assumes the 2 already-queued bcm.c patches for 5.15-stable have
landed by the time this is applied. If not, please let me know and I
will rebase.

Lee Jones (1):
  can: bcm: defer rx_op deallocation to workqueue to fix thrtimer UAF

Oliver Hartkopp (8):
  can: bcm: add locking when updating filter and timer values
  can: bcm: fix CAN frame rx/tx statistics
  can: bcm: extend bcm_tx_lock usage for data and timer updates
  can: bcm: validate frame length in bcm_rx_setup() for RTR replies
  can: bcm: add missing device refcount for CAN filter removal
  can: bcm: fix stale rx/tx ops after device removal
  can: bcm: fix data race on rx_stamp/rx_ifindex in bcm_rx_handler()
  can: bcm: track a single source interface for ANYDEV timeout/throttle
    ops

